														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4863673">
									

<blockquote>
<p>My concern is you don't really have a cohesive story around this so much as a weird DnD monster; and if you don't have the story down, this won't work.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So, I was thinking that for the story, someone would find a journal of the creature in that dimension and based on the notes there he would discover that the creature was once a human but it was transformed into this anomaly after having found this lantern. He became the lantern bearer and was corrupted by it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>why does this thing bother turning humans into wood in order to burn them in it's lantern instead of like, just using regular wood when it's in a forest?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Uhhh, I forgot to mention it’s an oil lantern. It needs oil to stay lit, not wood. When it transforms you, you’ll become a tree full of oil. Then it will use that oil to fuel the lantern. There is not source for oil in that dimension other than this.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>What does the history of its manifestations add?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I was thinking that it would add some nice background information, you know, make things more realistic, more believable.</p>

