<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Not until critiqued.</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article / Tale.</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Drama (Possibly something else, but I can't think of what it'd be.)</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> It'd begin as a tale. After a medium amount of writing in the tale, it'd then show an entry of the SCP - at least, what is understood about them at that point. Then switching back to tale, then after more is learnt, the document is updated again. Repeat this until the document is fully written, ending with a short note.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> An unexplained (yet theorized) scientific phenomena referred to as &quot;Earthquake lights&quot;. Strange lights that seem to appear in the skies whilst (usually high-magnitude) earthquakes form. However, what isn't expected is that these are entities made of light, appearing to simply spectate the earthquakes. Why they do this is found out in the tale.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> During a high-magnitude earthquake near Site [REDACTED], there were &quot;Earthquake Lights&quot; spotted by many people. As this is a scientifically unexplained phenomena, MTF Unit Rho-10 &quot;Shaken, Not Stirred&quot; (an MTF unit created to withstand seismic activity, or unnatural geological movement) enters the scene to investigate. After recordings are taken, and the film is placed through numerous filters &amp; analysations, it's found that each of these 'strobes' of light contain a nearly humanoid entity which seems to be watching the earthquakes. When another high-magnitude earthquake occurs near the same area within the next month, the same dispatch is sent to investigate these flashes of light closer. As the protagonist, codename &quot;Charlie-0&quot; (or C-0 by military alphabets) approaches towards the light, it seems to remain still for much longer than previous. They go to the top of the nearest destroyed building via an extremely long grappling hook and a lot of climbing. 23 minutes later, they arrive at the top, before the entity slowly floats down towards him. They take him somewhere - yet to be discovered. The man would slowly begin to communicate with these entities, finding out more and more about them - as the secrets reveal he continually updates the logs manually. Finally, when he's freed, he decides to watch one final earthquake with them. That's how it'd end, with a full log &amp; a destroyed city.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The fact that this could, hypothetically, be real is a big thing. Playing off of real world unexplained phenomena. Not to mention the fact it opens up as a tale-SCP has always caught my interest. A dangerous scenario (that being an earthquake) being traversed whilst also trying to gain intel on things which you can barely even see for more then a flash of a second is extremely difficult, and thrilling to read about.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> There is almost definitely some shit which I've messed up with the lore, as I am an idiot. Please feel free to be harsh in critique. Thank you!</p>

